+# Fraternity Row survey — 18 October 2026
+
+This is a **source survey**, supplemented by archived native tree transforms and old screenshots. A new rendered baseline and the required performance baseline have **not** run. Wildlife work currently owns the shared Source/Config freeze and engine slot.
+
+## Scope confirmed
+
+The editable project is `/Users/Stewart/Documents/Unreal Projects/SeniorSendoff`. The separate `/Users/Stewart/Projects/Senior sendoff` directory is not the Unreal checkout. The user wants to fill the existing grass on the Row side of the main house, **without making the map bigger**, and has now authorized removing the main-house parking lot. The proposal keeps the three existing Row houses and adds two inside the existing field, with the former lot becoming front lawns/approaches. The main house remains separate. This survey still describes existing source; the parking has not yet been removed in game. See `PARKING_REMOVAL.md`.
+
+## Existing street houses
+
+Coordinates below are the current C++ scene coordinates, in centimetres. South is toward the road (negative Y).
+
+| Plan ID | Current facade | Body X | Body Y | Current status |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| R1 | Red brick, west house | -18625 to -16175 | -2545 to -295 | Closed scenic block |
+| R2 | Clapboard, middle house | -15300 to -12500 | -2530 to -430 | Closed scenic block |
+| R3 | Brick, east house | -11350 to -8850 | -2600 to -400 | Closed scenic block |
+
+`HouseFraternityRow::Build` returns three planting exclusions reaching Y 100. These are not player boundaries. `HouseExterior.cpp` builds the legacy `ExteriorFraternityRow` batch with collision and shadows disabled. The current doors and windows sit on closed box bodies; they do not establish usable interiors. Current letter strokes depict real organizations and must be replaced by fictional combinations.
+
+## What occupies Y 100–4520 today
+
+| Area | Source and archived-transform finding |
+|---|---|
+| Behind R1 | Continuous west-field ground with an existing solid hedge at X -18800 +/-60 running through the parcel from Y -4100 northward (`StreetY(-2900)` includes the -1200 setback). Archived Big31 at (-18935,1611) and Small46 at (-18827,3806) are west of that hedge. The usable proposed yard stays east of the hedge, X >=-18740. No individual rear lot, shed, party scene or backyard room is generated by the Row builder. |
+| Behind R2 | Continuous west-field ground. No original tree root in this parcel in the archived Big/Small transform receipt; no individual backyard structures generated by the Row builder. |
+| Behind R3 | Continuous west-field ground. No original tree root in this parcel in the archived Big/Small receipt; no individual rear yard generated by the Row builder. |
+| Existing grass east of R3 | Existing field plants and two original roots: Big52 maple at (-6215,1596), Big2 oak at (-4200,1200). This space is north of the existing parking area, now released for removal. The grass remains the proposed house site; the old parking becomes front lawns and approaches. |
+| Northern edge | Existing wooden fence at Y 4520, X -19300 to -3900; existing opening X -7320 to -6780. Keep the fence, gate and woodland slope. |
+
+The west-field surface is existing raised ground, not empty air. `HouseWestField::RaisedHeight`, `Grade`, and frozen-zone rules remain authoritative. The generic near-nature grass scatter is concentrated farther east than the three old houses; Calder cover also excludes the frozen zone. Existing front foundation beds do not amount to designed rear yards. No current rendered claim is made about how every grass instance looks.
+
+Tree evidence: `Saved/CampusMasterWork/runs/p8z_reviews/Saved/WoodsPassReview/original_trees.csv`, associated with the required CRC `0f3b2bb7`. This archive locates roots; it does not prove current canopy clearance. New runtime CRC and visual checks remain required.
+
+## Nearby protected geometry and tests
+
+- Road: Y -5550 to -4150; house-side sidewalk: -4150 to -3900. Neither moves.
+- Main-house parking: X -7200 to -3700, Y -2500 to -300. **Now authorized for removal.** Its north mulch bed extends to Y -110, its dedicated entrance reaches the sidewalk, and lot props can extend east of the body rectangle. Removal must address all of these while retaining main-house pedestrian access.
+- Main-house west shrub line: around X -3660, through Y 1300. The proposal stays farther west.
+- Field ground probes: X {-17500,-12500,-7000,-4400}, Y {2100,2800,3700}; every point and tolerance remains unchanged.
+- Fixed walking route: (-4500,2900), (-5700,3200), (-7050,3800), (-7050,4200), (-7050,4830), (-7050,5480), (-6800,5900). The proposed divider at X -6200 has an opening covering the crossing near Y 3422.
+- A street-side original tree at (-8356,-3800) rules out the initially considered access line X -8350. Revised access uses X -8100.
+- The unchanged west hedge is solid scene geometry (`Boundary()`), distinct from the disabled invisible PropertyBoundary. Retain it. Do not pretend its western strip is accessible from the R1 backyard.
+- The new ground-conforming dirt path overlaps fixed probe (-7000,3700). Its treatment must be noncolliding visual wear at current grade; no raised paving or terrain change is permitted there.
+- Do not append new planting exclusions to the three old NoGo boxes or consume the existing plant RNG differently. A changed exclusion can change tree transforms elsewhere.
+
+## What reads fake or empty
+
+Source inspection and the October 12 archived `final/*.png` show three closely related monumental porticos without different household lives. Their closed bodies prevent the exploration the brief asks for. The rear field lacks a sequence of individual occupied yards, service buildings, and gradual overgrowth. The redesign should replace repetition with five distinct households, while retaining the current terrain and trees. Those old images are historical context, **not** the required new before images.
+
+## Baseline still to capture
+
+After the wildlife owner releases the source/engine freeze and the brief's 20-minute idle condition is met: capture the current road, each rear yard, proposed infill, maple/oak clearances, existing gate and fence. Append new `detail_row_*` views at the end of the fixed exterior camera list, preserving every existing view and keeping new views outside planting exclusion/RNG logic. Run `Saved/CalderWork/tools/perf_ab.sh` before enabling any Row geometry changes. Record exact source hashes and current review verdicts with those captures.
+
+`SURVEY_SOURCE_RECEIPT.json` records the inspected source/map hashes. It is not a render, performance result, or saved-map acceptance.
